meta {
  name: 04 - PDF Extractor - Extract Text Only
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/runs/wait
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "assistant_id": "pdf_extractor",
    "input": {
      "pdf_base64": ""
    }
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:2024
}

docs {
  Uses POST /runs/wait: a stateless, synchronous run (creates an ephemeral
  thread internally, runs it to completion, returns the final state - no
  need to create a thread yourself first).
  
  The pdf_base64 above is a tiny 1-page PDF with real embedded text (no
  scanned image), generated with PyMuPDF, containing the lines:
    "Hello Bruno API test - invoice no. 12345"
    "Vendor: Acme Co.   Total: 999.00 THB"
  
  Since it has an embedded text layer, extract_pdf_text takes the fast path
  (no OCR/Tesseract needed), so this works even without Ollama - verified
  against this branch's pdf_extractor graph on 2026-09-16.
  
  No form_template_base64 was given, so the graph stops after extraction
  (see the _route_after_extract branch in src/agent/pdf_graph.py) - the
  quote-to-form steps (which need the Gemma cloud model) never run.
  
  Expected response shape: {pdf_base64, text, pages[], page_count,
  ocr_page_count, embedded_text_page_count, warnings[], error: null}
}
